AUDIO: 'Sup guys, Laura Tech here with another video for you all. Today we are covering LTX 2.5 using Simplegen. This model is super fast with generation times for 10 second clips at an astonishing 30 seconds to 1 minute on'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'average. And if you haven\'t noticed already, I\'m not actually Laura Tech. He made me with LTX 2.5 on Simplegen. So he\'s going to take over from here now. Stay tuned to see how you can make'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'videos just like this. &gt;&gt; So all of those videos that you just saw were generated locally on my 5090 through Simplegen using LTX 2.5. If you didn\'t gather that from those clips. The'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model came out just days ago. If you\'ve never seen Simplegen before, I\'ve got a full walk through of the application linked in the description. Go watch that video if you want to get an idea of what Simplegen actually is a little bit more in depth. But the too long didn\'t read'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for that video is basically this. Simplegen strips ComfyUI down to buttons and drop downs and you\'re not wiring nodes, you\'re not managing checkpoints by hand. You\'re just picking a preset and hitting generate and getting the same exact output that you would get'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from using a professional ComfyUI node graph. As a matter of fact, Simplegen actually uses ComfyUI and just wraps it up and does the generation through their super intuitive UI. Now here\'s why Simplegen actually gives you an'

[01:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'advantage for a model like LTX 2.5 that just came out a few days ago. So LTX 2.5 is brand new, a couple days old, maybe a week at this time. And anytime a model this size drops, the first week or two on raw ComfyUI is pretty rough. There\'s'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'missing nodes, there\'s broken dependencies, there\'s VRAM settings that have not been optimized yet, custom node conflicts, and so on. And Simplegen literally skips all of that. The preset is already built, already tested,'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'already configured for your hardware. You basically just install it and you generate. That\'s the actual advantage of using it over ComfyUI for brand new model releases. So we\'re going to head over to the preset store and get LTX 2.5. I have not installed it yet, so'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let\'s go ahead and do that together. So we\'re going to click in the LTX 2.5 and you get two variants here that you can see. So, there\'s the balanced int8 Comfra which needs about 16 GB of VRAM to be comfortable, but there are people'

[02:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'who are getting generations with just 8 GB of VRAM. And then there\'s the full precision BF16 model which says it needs about 48 GB of VRAM, but that\'s not true because I\'ve used it on my device locally through ComfyUI and I\'m running'

[02:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '32 GB of VRAM. I think with about 24 GB of VRAM you should be okay to use the large model, but I\'m just going to use the int8 Comfra version. And you can see that we get both text to video and image'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to video. So, let\'s go ahead and install the preset. Now, we\'re going to head over to the generate tab at the top of the left-hand menu and we\'re going to go to video and we are going to select the LTX 2.5 preset that we have just downloaded. Now, we have text to video'

[02:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and we have image to video. I\'m going to test image to video first. So, after selecting image to video, I\'m just going to scroll down on the right-hand side here and install the preset locally. Now, here\'s the step that people are going to hit and not expect. LTX 2.5\'s'

[02:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'weights hit a negated Hugging Face repository. That means before you can install this preset, you need to go to the repository page and accept Latrix\'s license and add a Hugging Face key inside of this SimplyGen setting here.'

[03:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s a one-time thing and it\'s free, but you can\'t skip it. I\'m going to walk you through the steps on navigating through the Hugging Face menus in order to give access to LTX 2.5. So, first things first, go on to Hugging Face. I\'ll leave'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a link in the description to their official website, create an account and then search for LTX in the search bar as you see here and select the top result LTX 2.5. And once you open up the repository for LTX 2.5, you should see'

[03:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the gated model option highlighted on screen now. Mine says you have already been granted access to this model, but yours will not say that obviously. Just click the accept button and you\'ll give access to the model. Next, in the top'

[03:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right corner, you\'re going to click your profile icon and you should see access tokens highlighted on screen here. Go Go and open up that menu. Then you will see the access tokens menu with a create new token option in the top right corner of'

[03:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that. Go ahead and click create new token. And then in the create new access token menu, you\'re going to have to define a token name. You can write anything here. And you\'re going to have to select the read-only preset. After clicking read-only and setting a token'

[04:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'name, you\'re going to go ahead and scroll down to the bottom and click create token. And that is the token that you will paste into your Simply Gen menu. All right, so the model is fully downloaded, but as always, I feel the need to go into a little bit of depth'

[04:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about how prompting works for the model that we\'re using. Because we\'re using Simply Gen, we don\'t have a ton of different settings to change within our workflow. There\'s no fancy node graphs, no sliders that we can change, which is great and super convenient. But that'

[04:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'puts a lot of weight on using the proper formatting for prompts. Since the prompt is one of the only variables that we really need to worry about, it\'s important that you make sure that you get a good prompt. So I\'ll leave a link in the description to the official LTX'

[04:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'repository and their prompt guidance and how they want you to write prompts, but I can also just tell you. So LTX 2.5 wants one flowing paragraph, present tense, not a comma-separated tag list.'

[04:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That\'s the single biggest habit people carry over from image generation and it actually hurts your results here. So you just want to cover the basics in that paragraph. So what\'s happening, who\'s in the shot, what the camera\'s doing, and what you want to hear. And it\'s'

[05:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'important that you describe what you want to hear because LTX generates the audio in the same pass. So if you don\'t describe sound, you\'re leaving it to chance. And in the more advanced options here, we can see that there is a negative prompt. But my advice to you is to keep that negative prompt short and'

[05:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'concise and really nail down the few things that you do not want in your generations. So 5 to 15 words is the sweet spot. So here\'s our reference photo and I have come up with a nice detailed prompt on exactly what\'s going'

[05:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to be going on in the video based on our reference photo. We are not generating dialogue for this pass, so I\'m going to leave that off for now. And for the resolution, I\'m going to do 720p to to out. And I\'m going to crank the duration'

[05:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'up to 7 seconds. Actually, let\'s do 8 seconds. And that\'s it. That\'s genuinely how easy it is. So, let\'s just generate. All right, let\'s check the generation out. Wow. Wow, okay. That actually came out'

[06:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so much better than I was expecting it to. Wow, I\'m actually very pleasantly surprised. And guys, check out this generation time. To get a clip of this quality in 34 seconds is absolutely insane. Like, I don\'t think you guys'

[06:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'understand. At 720p for an 8-second clip, getting something at this quality in 34 seconds is completely unheard of. LTX has absolutely crushed it with this one. I genuinely don\'t know how they'

[06:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'managed that, but it\'s insane how fast this generates. So, next up, we\'re going to do a generation that does some basic physics and speed tests and actually push this model towards its limits. So, we\'re going to animate this photo that'

[06:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we have on screen now. And what this generation is going to allow us to test is whether we get slow motion output, which is something that video generation models typically struggle with. Usually when describing a fast-paced scene, for whatever reason, the models just default'

[06:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to generating a slow-motion video. So, we\'re going to put that to the test right now. Yeah, so just as I expected, we are getting some slow motion here, but I actually didn\'t describe any type of real-time motion within the prompt. So,'

[07:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m going to do that and I\'m also going to include slow motion in the negative prompt to see if we can actually get full-speed motion without having to fight with the prompt too much. Because typically, when you\'re getting slow motion outputs with video models, as of the recent past few releases of video'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'models, you have to fight with the prompt for hours and you might not even get the result that you\'re looking for. So, let\'s see how easy it is with LTX 2.5. Couldn\'t have gotten much easier than'

[07:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that. I mean, I literally wrote two words in the positive prompt and one word in the negative prompt. Really impressed. All right, so what our next generation here aims to do is I want to test how well it does with physics like water'

[07:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that are a bit more complex to actually get looking good. A lot of previous video models have struggled with this immensely and no matter what you prompt and no matter what settings you change, you just never seem to be able to get the water to actually have good flowing'

[07:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'realistic look with real textures. So let\'s test that out. So while the water does look really good, I actually did keep the negative prompt regarding slow motion in there and it'

[08:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'didn\'t listen to it. So I\'m going to try another attempt and actually try to bake in the real-time motion into the positive prompt here as well and we\'ll see what happens. So yeah, honestly I\'ve tried like three or four different'

[08:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompt variations with increasing intensity regarding the slow motion and I just have not been able to get it. So it\'s unfortunate to see that LTX 2.5 still struggles with this, but what can'

[08:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you do? So if you watched the last video that I did on Minimax H3, the image to video results that we got were not that good. But I am pleasantly surprised with the image to video results that LTX 2.5 has given us. But we\'re going to go'

[08:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ahead into the LTX 2.5 text to video and we are going to test that out. So within Simply Gen, the creators have blessed us with a character dialogue option that you wouldn\'t normally find within your average run-of-the-mill comfy UI'

[08:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workflow. But we have it on Simply Gen and we\'re going to put it to use. But first, I want to turn this off and I want to try putting the dialogue in the prompt and then testing the dialogue feature that is unique to Simply Gen in a separate generation to see which one'

[09:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gives us better results. &gt;&gt; Anyway, I was wondering if you have an answer to my question. Is mayonnaise an instrument? &gt;&gt; So honestly, overall not bad at all, but we can see that there\'s a little pause'

[09:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there at the end in between parts of the dialogue. So now we\'re going to use the built-in Simply Gen feature and let\'s see how that works. So now I am going to extract the dialogue from the original prompt, turn on the option within Simply'

[09:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Gen, paste that in there, fix up our prompt a little bit, and generate again. &gt;&gt; Anyway, I was wondering if you have an answer to my question. Is mayonnaise an instrument? &gt;&gt; So, overall, I think that the SimplyGen'

[09:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'feature for dialogue is much better. It seems more natural, the voice sounds better, and it comes off as more natural flowing. So, I think that\'s a W for SimplyGen\'s character dialogue feature.'

